.Dd August 1, 2026
.Dt INTEGRIS-VERIFY-CONFIG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm integris-verify-config
.Nd validate an Integris configuration document without side effects
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl config Ar path.json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
parses and validates an Integris configuration JSON document according to
.Pa docs/specifications/configuration.md
and prints:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
the configuration digest as
.Li digest_sha256= Ns Ar hex
.It
the canonical JSON as
.Li canonical_json= Ns Ar json
.El
.Pp
The tool performs no network I/O, archive mutation, key use, journal write, or
authority acquisition.
Invalid documents produce no product side effect.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width "-config path"
.It Fl config Ar path.json
Path to the configuration document (required).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Document is valid; digest and canonical JSON were printed.
.It 1
Read or parse failure.
.It 2
Missing
.Fl config
or usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
integris-verify-config -config path/to/config.json
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr integris 7 ,
.Xr integrisd 8
.Pp
.Pa docs/specifications/configuration.md
.Sh HISTORY
Added so operators and CI can validate configuration immutability properties
before any product authority exists.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Integris contributors
.Sh CAVEATS
A valid document is necessary but not sufficient for a safe deployment.
Session binding and confinement checks occur only in the future daemon path.
